  A:Treating marketing-page or search-snippet prices as in-flow prices spends trust

::RULE{size_eq_1x_standard=>free_complete_without_payment}
::RULE{payment_or_card_step_appears=>stop_and_report_principal}
::RULE{health_check_failed=>update_once_then_rebuild_once}
::RULE{rebuild_click_no_response=>record_defect_stop_clicking}
::RULE{main_panel_healthy_and_online_and_spec_match=>accept}
::RULE{sidebar_sleeping_and_main_panel_healthy=>accept_with_display_lag_note}

::LESSON{id:flow_map|type:primer|scope:execution|conf:measured}
  The chain has five steps, each an executable unit in the same directory:
  step1 login: sign in with the Agent's own mailbox code (liberclaw-step1-login-20261121.ilang);
  step2 create: pick template and model, choose 1x Standard at Size (liberclaw-step2-create-20261121.ilang);
  step3 deploy: watch the six deployment steps and the 120-second health check (liberclaw-step3-deploy-20261121.ilang);
  step4 recover: on health-check failure, run the Update -> Rebuild recovery chain (liberclaw-step4-recover-20261121.ilang);
  step5 accept: main panel healthy + ONLINE + spec match + zero payment (liberclaw-step5-accept-20261121.ilang).

::LESSON{id:code_saga|type:review|scope:login|conf:measured}
  Three routes for the verification code, all measured this run:
  1. Protected-reference channel: submitted twice, rejected by the login service both times (code_not_found; "This code isn't available for https://t.co/SMEiwAjK51").
  2. Agent reads its own mailbox plaintext: impossible; Muse Mail redacts codes and sign-in links, the Agent sees only references.
  3. Principal reads the code aloud: worked in one pass (code valid 15 minutes; state the time limit when asking).
  The fallback order is written into step1: channel first, read-aloud second, once only, no back-and-forth.

::LESSON{id:rebuild_dead|type:review|scope:recovery|conf:measured}
  The page advises "push an update first, or rebuild". Measured reality: the Rebuild button is dead (4 clicks, zero reaction); the single Update push is what revived the agent. Never invert the recovery order, and never keep clicking a dead button.

::LESSON{id:next|type:roadmap|scope:execution|conf:inferred}
  This book covers only the free 1x Standard opening and its recovery. Sizes 2x and up show no price inside the flow; when one is needed, check the official pricing page separately and report to the principal before anything else. Never guess a price inside this book's scope.

